And here's an example implementation of a class that implements `Person`:

```
public class Employee implements Person {
   private String name;
   private int age;

   public Employee(String name, int age) {
      this.name = name;
      this.age = age;
   }

   @Override
   public String getName() {
      return this.name;
   }

   @Override
   public int getAge() {
      return this.age;
   }

   @Override
   public void setName(String name) {
      this.name = name;
   }

   @Override
   public void setAge(int age) {
      this.age = age;
   }
}
```

This is just one example of how you could implement a `Person` interface in Java. Other programming languages may have different syntax or conventions for defining interfaces and classes, but the basic idea should be similar.

